- Queued the last 6 eval cells: the text QA set (MRQA) at seed 43, plus the multi-passage text set (HotpotQA, reported but not deciding) at both seeds. Each runs as a frozen/reference pair, set to start when its seed's finetune ends.
- The eval code is byte-identical to the earlier queued cells, so every pair is scored by the same code.
- The verifier found no unsupported claims. I added one caveat it raised: the early 300-document previews were scored against reference results written by older eval code.

**Running now**
- Frozen finetune seed 42 ends about 16:20; seed 43 about 16:50.
- 18 jobs follow them: 2 checks that the frozen weights did not move, and 16 eval cells (documents, photos, MRQA, HotpotQA × 2 seeds × frozen/reference).

**Next wake**
- It fires when all 18 jobs have finished (at most 9 h from now).
- It will confirm each cell's exit code and settings, then run the paired comparison: judge-accuracy differences per question, with a 95% confidence interval (CI).
- It will apply the gate: the frozen side must be within 2 points of the reference on documents, photos and MRQA at both seeds, with the CI not wholly below 0.
- It will also re-run the unit tests on the committed code. They passed earlier, but on an uncommitted copy. This wake had used all 6 of its allowed submissions.

**Tooling gap logged:** expmon does not store the environment variables that define an eval cell (image budget, chunk length, pages per question). So the MRQA and HotpotQA cells look identical in the campaign's table of runs.

